It is the standard 'trees' dataset. See help(trees) in R.

It may be a bug here in readNexus:

    if (type == "tree" || length(tipdata) == 0 ) {
        output <- trees
    }

that 'trees' is returned from the global environment rather than the local
tree structure that may have gotten filled.
 
| Lastly, is there a way to control the output though Rcpp or otherwise, a
| fair bit of what appears to be stderr gets printed in the R console, it'd
| be nice to control this.

Sure. From C++ I use things like this 

// simple logging help
inline void logTxtFunction(const char* file, const int line, const char* expression); 

#ifndef logTxt
//#define logTxt(x) logTxtFunction(__FILE__, __LINE__, x);
#define logTxt(x) 
#endif

If you undef the first form of logTxt(x) then the logging macros gets activated.

Hth,  Dirk
 
